WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Ephesus.

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.630
A busy port, home of
the Temple of Artemis.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.870
Paul taught here for two years.

4
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.140
Then the silversmiths,
who sold Artemis shrines,

5
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.750
started a riot.

6
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.330
Later, a letter comes from a
prisoner, an ambassador in chains.

7
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.700
It says God has already seated its readers
with Christ in the heavenly places.

8
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.740
Yet near the end: put on
the whole armour of God.

9
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.190
So why would people seated
in heaven need armour?

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.640
In this mission, you'll
weigh up who wrote it,

11
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.780
and to whom.

12
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:37.960
Then you'll trace its plan of salvation,
its household code and its armour.

13
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: find out why a letter that
seats readers in heaven hands them armour.
